  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 201 PM MDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nSaturday...Southwest flow aloft prevails. Looks like with a \nminor stream of the monsoonal moisture tap, we anticipate \nisolated to widely scattered showers and thunderstorms in the \nafternoon and evening.\n\nSunday...The precipitable water values increase somewhat as \nmonsoonal moisture increases. With that said, expect scattered \nafternoon showers and thunderstorms to form over and near our \nSnowy Range and Laramie Range in the afternoon due to orographic\neffects and differential heating, with most of the convection \npropagating over the Nebraska Panhandle in the evening.\n\nMonday...Somewhat drier air aloft moves overhead under \nsouthwest flow aloft, which should correspond to an areal \ndecrease in afternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms.\n\nTuesday and Wednesday...Again, somewhat drier air infiltrates \nour western counties using precipitable water values, with a bit\nbetter moisture further east, thus isolated to scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms expected mainly over the mountains and\neastward.",
